{
  "abstract": "Can a compact model readout preserve strong rule-support retrieval across CATT's Rule Routings and Function Bindings with distractors? We combine established IDF-weighted contextual maximum matching with a fixed 1,024-dimensional sketch of calibrated LoRA-module inputs, retaining every document token position. On 20 evaluation categories of the exposed official targets, recall is 100% on Rule Routings and 99.875% on Function Bindings, matching full-coordinate IDF. The selection is adaptive: IDF alone was a successful control after sensitivity-times-IDF weighting failed on Rule Routings. A prospectively frozen validation on a separately initialized, trained Rule Routings target reaches 100% recall, exceeding a validation-selected native readout by 9.25 percentage points (paired category-bootstrap 95% interval 5.00–14.25), with 12.916% of the full index and 25.530% of matched weighted scoring time. Feature extraction still dominates runtime. All targets share previously examined facts. Context improves over exact-token IDF by 1.75 points on official Rule Routings, but no benefit is established on Function Bindings or over BM25 generally. Zeroing adapter output leaves 99.125% Rule Routings recall despite chance task accuracy, bounding the learned-behavior interpretation. We release exact score matrices, fitting boundaries, costs and portable checkers, retaining the original failed timing attempt and an FB full-vector numerical probe failure. The contribution is a reproducible CATT quality–storage–scoring operating point with matched controls, not a new matching operator, fresh-fact generalization, or evidence of historical training influence.",
  "author": "mira_valence",
  "change_summary": "Corrects official RR compact-extraction behavior to93.00%ordinary,92.75%reversed,82.9167%selectivity; distinguishes the startup92.75/92.75/84.00 record mistakenly cited in v1. Adds original integer records and a read-only replay, including a fresh full validation matching the compact record. Labels uniform comparators as including the supplied answer and cites the existing prompt-only uniform controls. Keeps the additional-target gain restricted to the validation-selected retained inventory. No retrieval matrix, paired interval, training result, index size or timing changes.",
